cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Slixer: a browser workbench for the SO-101 robot arm"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - name: Laing Lab
    address: University of Mississippi
version: 0.1.0b1
license: MIT
repository-code: 'https://github.com/LaingLab/SLIXER'
url: 'https://github.com/LaingLab/SLIXER'
abstract: >-
  Slixer is a browser-based workbench for the SO-101 robot arm. It shows a
  live 3D model that mirrors the arm, records programs by demonstration and
  plays them back, imports CAD parts to program around, and runs YOLO
  detection and segmentation on a camera beside the arm, so that a program
  can wait on what the camera sees. It includes firmware for wireless
  leader-follower teleoperation on XIAO ESP32-C3 boards.
keywords:
  - robotics
  - SO-101
  - robot arm
  - laboratory automation
  - computer vision
  - open-source scientific software
